/*QUAKED func_bobbing (0 0.5 0.8) ? START_OFF CRUSHER_NO_REVERSE NON_SOLID STOP_AT_POS2_WHEN_TURNED_OFF STOP_AT_MIDPOINT_WHEN_TURNED_OFF STOP_AT_POS1_WHEN_TURNED_OFF RANDOM_PHASE START_INVISIBLE NOT_ON_EASY NOT_ON_NORMAL NOT_ON_HARD NOT_IN_DEATHMATCH
Bobbing por from alkaline/dp300 by Rel71  29/oct/2026

Moves on a cosine wave between pos1 and pos2 and back, once every wait seconds. By default pos1 is the position where it was built and pos2 is pos1 minus distance along angle. If pos1 or pos2 is set, angle and distance are ignored and both are used as given. They are values for the entity origin: offsets from the built position for a brush without an origin brush, world positions otherwise. The phase comes from absolute time, so movers with the same wait stay in sync. Setting mdl replaces the brush with that alias model.
Triggering it toggles it on and off. With a stop flag it keeps moving until it reaches that position; with several, it stops at the first one reached.

-------- KEYS --------
"angle" Direction.
"targetname" Name.
"wait" Period (seconds). Default: 4.
"distance" Travel distance. Default: 64.
"delay" Starting phase (0-1). Default: 0.
0 starts at pos1, 0.5 at pos2. Ignored with the random phase flag.
"pos1" pos1 origin (X Y Z).
"pos2" pos2 origin (X Y Z).
"dmg" Damage when blocked. Default: 2.
"mdl" Alias model to display (always non-solid).
"alpha" Alpha (empty or 0 = opaque).

-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
START_OFF (1) : Start off
CRUSHER_NO_REVERSE (2) : Crusher (no reverse)
NON_SOLID (4) : Non-solid
STOP_AT_POS2_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (8) : Stop at pos2 when turned off
STOP_AT_MIDPOINT_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (16) : Stop at midpoint when turned off
STOP_AT_POS1_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (32) : Stop at pos1 when turned off
RANDOM_PHASE (64) : Random phase. Overrides delay.
START_INVISIBLE (128) : Start invisible. Spawns on the first trigger. Later triggers toggle it.
NOT_ON_EASY (256) : Not on Easy
NOT_ON_NORMAL (512) : Not on Normal
NOT_ON_HARD (1024) : Not on Hard
NOT_IN_DEATHMATCH (2048) : Not in Deathmatch
*/

/*QUAKED func_bobbing_fade (0 0.5 0.8) ? START_OFF CRUSHER_NO_REVERSE SOLID STOP_AT_POS2_WHEN_TURNED_OFF STOP_AT_MIDPOINT_WHEN_TURNED_OFF STOP_AT_POS1_WHEN_TURNED_OFF RANDOM_PHASE START_INVISIBLE NOT_ON_EASY NOT_ON_NORMAL NOT_ON_HARD NOT_IN_DEATHMATCH
Bobbing mover with distance fade made by Rel71 29/oct/2026

Same movement and trigger behavior as func_bobbing. Its alpha is interpolated between alpha_near and alpha_far by the distance from the nearest living player to the entity's bounding box, so it is 0 anywhere inside it. Non-solid by default. Meant for fog volumes.
While it is outside the player's PVS it stops moving, and it resumes at the same phase when visible again.
Alpha 0 renders opaque in the network protocol, so the computed alpha never goes below 0.001 (invisible). An alpha_near of 0 becomes 0.001 and an alpha_far of 0 becomes 1.

-------- KEYS --------
"angle" Direction.
"targetname" Name.
"wait" Period (seconds). Default: 4.
"distance" Travel distance. Default: 64.
"delay" Starting phase (0-1). Default: 0.
0 starts at pos1, 0.5 at pos2. Ignored with the random phase flag.
"pos1" pos1 origin (X Y Z).
"pos2" pos2 origin (X Y Z).
"dmg" Damage when blocked. Default: 2.
"mdl" Alias model to display (always non-solid).
"alpha_near" Alpha at dist_near or closer. Default: 0.001.
"alpha_far" Alpha at dist_far or farther. Default: 1.
"dist_near" Distance where the fade ends. Default: 96.
"dist_far" Distance where alpha_far is reached (default dist_near + 256).
"flicker_amp" Flicker amount (0 = off, 0.15 = +/-15%). Default: 0.
"flicker_rate" Flicker cycles per second. Default: 0.4.
The think runs at 10 Hz at most, so values above 1 look stroboscopic.

-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
START_OFF (1) : Start off
CRUSHER_NO_REVERSE (2) : Crusher (no reverse)
SOLID (4) : Solid. Brush only. An alias model set in mdl is always non-solid.
STOP_AT_POS2_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (8) : Stop at pos2 when turned off
STOP_AT_MIDPOINT_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (16) : Stop at midpoint when turned off
STOP_AT_POS1_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (32) : Stop at pos1 when turned off
RANDOM_PHASE (64) : Random phase. Overrides delay.
START_INVISIBLE (128) : Start invisible. Spawns on the first trigger. Later triggers toggle it.
NOT_ON_EASY (256) : Not on Easy
NOT_ON_NORMAL (512) : Not on Normal
NOT_ON_HARD (1024) : Not on Hard
NOT_IN_DEATHMATCH (2048) : Not in Deathmatch
*/

/*QUAKED misc_bobbing (0 0.5 0.8) (-8 -8 -8) (8 8 8) START_OFF - - STOP_AT_POS2_WHEN_TURNED_OFF STOP_AT_MIDPOINT_WHEN_TURNED_OFF STOP_AT_POS1_WHEN_TURNED_OFF RANDOM_PHASE START_INVISIBLE NOT_ON_EASY NOT_ON_NORMAL NOT_ON_HARD NOT_IN_DEATHMATCH
{
model({ "path": mdl });
}
Bobbing alias model
function restored by Rel71 29/oct/2026
Point version of func_bobbing for the model set in mdl, which is required. Same movement, keys and trigger behavior. Always non-solid.

-------- KEYS --------
"angle" Direction.
"targetname" Name.
"wait" Period (seconds). Default: 4.
"distance" Travel distance. Default: 64.
"delay" Starting phase (0-1). Default: 0.
0 starts at pos1, 0.5 at pos2. Ignored with the random phase flag.
"pos1" pos1 origin (X Y Z).
"pos2" pos2 origin (X Y Z).
"dmg" Damage when blocked. Default: 2.
"mdl" Alias model to display (always non-solid).
"alpha" Alpha (empty or 0 = opaque).

-------- SPAWNFLAGS --------
START_OFF (1) : Start off
STOP_AT_POS2_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (8) : Stop at pos2 when turned off
STOP_AT_MIDPOINT_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (16) : Stop at midpoint when turned off
STOP_AT_POS1_WHEN_TURNED_OFF (32) : Stop at pos1 when turned off
RANDOM_PHASE (64) : Random phase. Overrides delay.
START_INVISIBLE (128) : Start invisible. Spawns on the first trigger. Later triggers toggle it.
NOT_ON_EASY (256) : Not on Easy
NOT_ON_NORMAL (512) : Not on Normal
NOT_ON_HARD (1024) : Not on Hard
NOT_IN_DEATHMATCH (2048) : Not in Deathmatch
*/

